You’re talking about reciprocal happiness.

It’s not enough to be happy with the life you’ve built. You want the people sharing that life to be happy they’ve got you, too.

And there’s a beautiful tension in that:

* Gratitude: Appreciate what you’ve got.
* Ambition: Keep becoming more than you are.
* Stewardship: Make what you’ve got better because you’re part of it.
* Reciprocity: Make sure you’re loved and appreciated in return.

But there’s another layer.

What you’ve got includes yourself. And you’ve gotta be happy with you, too.

You can be grateful without settling. You can improve without believing you’re inadequate. You can give people your best without making your worth dependent on their approval.

Maybe that’s the trick:

Build a life you’re happy to have, become someone who’s a joy to have around, and surround yourself with people who feel the same way about you.

Not just having a good life. Being good for the life you have.